  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pawan Kumar Saini vs The State Of Bihar on 12 January, 2023 Author: Anjani Kumar Sharan Bench: Anjani Kumar Sharan In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.63211 of 2022 Arising Out of Ps. Case No.-146 Year-2010 Thana- Government Official District- Bhagalpur ====================================================== Pawan Kumar Saini Son of Kalu Ram R/o- W-8, Gram- Nimki, Shastri Nagar, New Delhi ... ... Pet Versus The State of Bihar ... ... Opposite Party/s ====================================================== Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr.Manoj Kumar Jha, Adv. For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Dr.Mrityunjaya Kr.Gautam, App ===================================================== = Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Anjani Kumar Sharan Oral Order",
    "facts": "The petitioner is apprehending his arrest in a case registered for the offence punishable under Sections 16(i)(a) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955 pending in the learned court below.",
    "arguments": "As per the prosecution case, the informant, Food Inspector, alleging on 16.11.2009 at 1:30 P.M. visited the place of occurrence and took sample of 'chana dal' which was sent for chemical analysis and in the chemical analysis sample of 'chana dal' was found sub-standard and adulterous in quality. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the petitioner is innocent and has been falsely implicated in this Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.63211 of 2022(2) dt.12-01-2023 case. He submits that there is no specific overt act against the petitioner. He further submits that similarly situated other co- accused person has already been granted bail by the learned lower court itself and Section 82 Cr.P.C. has been issued against the petitioner. He submits that the summon is not received by the petitioner because he is living in Delhi. He further submits that petitioner has got one criminal antecedent as stated in para- 3 of the bail application.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "As per the prosecution case, the informant, Food Inspector, alleging on 16.11.2009 at 1:30 P.M. visited the place of occurrence and took sample of 'chana dal' which was sent for chemical analysis and in the chemical analysis sample of 'chana dal' was found sub-standard and adulterous in quality. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the petitioner is innocent and has been falsely implicated in this Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.63211 of 2022(2) dt.12-01-2023 case. He submits that there is no specific overt act against the petitioner. He further submits that similarly situated other co- accused person has already been granted bail by the learned lower court itself and Section 82 Cr.P.C. has been issued against the petitioner. He submits that the summon is not received by the petitioner because he is living in Delhi. He further submits that petitioner has got one criminal antecedent as stated in para- 3 of the bail application.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
